      },
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "markdown": "# 🌍 Plate Tectonics\n\n## Earth is alive beneath our feet\n\nEarth's rigid outer shell is divided into enormous moving slabs called **tectonic plates**.\n\nDriven by deep heat and the slow churn of the mantle, these plates drift, collide, separate, and slide past one another.\n\nTheir motion opens oceans, raises mountain ranges, feeds volcanoes, carves trenches, and releases the tremendous energy of earthquakes.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1785000968209,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "6d7a9d2c-7b4f-4d61-9f0d-4b8f279a51e3"
        }
      }
    },
